# Official National Park Service web pages of Gettysburg National Military Park (www.nps.gov/gett/learn/historyculture/): finding aids of the park's monument files (state memorials, the Confederate Soldiers and Sailors Monument, the Pennsylvania Memorial, the Lincoln Speech Memorial), fetched 2026-11-16.
# Each page lists, in date order, archival letters, programs and press clippings of the park's monument file with a short summary; a line of a finding aid supports exactly what it says (the date of a program, a planned date, the site named). Every monument here is a later feature (use none): it is never drawn in the July 1863 scene. Where the page gives two dates for one ceremony both are carried (certainty conflict).
# Workstream bt-web, task nps-landscape, third milestone.

@ NPSGOV-HC-ALABAMA-MONUMENT
